64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,1,"Signal Processing: Image Communication 108 (2022) 116827 Contents lists available at ScienceDirect Signal Processing: Image Communication journal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/image KOHTD: Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset Nazgul Toiganbayevaa,1, Mahmoud Kasemc,d,1, Galymzhan Abdimanapb,c,1, Kairat Bostanbekovb,c,1, Abdelrahman Abdallahd,1,, Anel Alimovab,c,1, Daniyar Nurseitovb,c,1 aAl-Farabi Kazakh National University, Almaty, 050040, Kazakhstan bKazMunayGas Engineering LLP, Nur-Sultan, 010000, Kazakhstan cSatbayev University, Almaty, 050013, Kazakhstan dInformation Technology Department, Assiut University, Assiut, 71515, Assiut, Egypt A R T I C L E I N F O Keywords: Document analysis and recognition Handwritten Kazakh text recognition in Cyrillic Benchmark dataset Convolutional neural networks Genetic algorithm Deep learningA B S T R A C T Despite the transition to digital information exchange, many documents, such as invoices, taxes, memos and questionnaires, historical data, and answers to exam questions, still require handwritten inputs."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,2,"In this regard, there is a need to implement Handwritten Text Recognition (HTR) which is an automatic way to decrypt records using a computer. Handwriting recognition is challenging because of the virtually infinite number of ways a person can write the same message. For this proposal we introduce Kazakh handwritten text recognition research, a comprehensive dataset of Kazakh handwritten texts is necessary. This is particularly true given the lack of a dataset for handwritten Kazakh text. In this paper, we proposed our extensive Kazakh offline Handwritten Text dataset (KOHTD), which has 3000 handwritten exam papers and more than 140335 segmented images and there are approximately 922010 symbols. It can serve researchers in the field of handwriting recognition tasks by using deep and machine learning. We used a variety of popular text recognition methods for word and line recognition in our studies, including CTC-based and attention-based methods."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,3,"In this paper, we have implemented state-of-the-art deep learning-based methods for Handwriting recognition for KOHTD dataset to create several strong baselines. The findings demonstrate KOHTDs diversity. Also, we proposed a Genetic Algorithm (GA) for line and word segmentation based on random enumeration of a parameter. The dataset and GA code are available at https://github.com/abdoelsayed2016/KOHTD. 1. Introduction Deep learning has been widely used in several fields nowadays, such as Medical applications like Cancers diagnoses, detection, and classification [1], image captioning [2], speech recognition [3] and in medical question answers [46], table detection and recognition [7,8] also deep learning has been used in software engineering such as optimizing the time and schedule of the software projects [9,10] and one of the most usages of Deep Learning is handwritten recognition for different languages as we will discuss."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,4,"For some types of images, automatic recognition of handwritten texts is still a challenging issue in spite of the recent improvements of the recognition methods and systems, in recent years, handwritten text recognition is attracting more researchers to work on it. Comprehensive and unbounded handwritten datasets are gaining more importance than before, handwritten text can be found: handwritten notes, memos, whiteboards, medical records, historical documents, stylus input text, etc. Therefore, support for understanding the handwritten text in images needs to be provided in a full OCR solution. For several languages Corresponding author. E-mail address: abdelrahmanelsayed@aun.edu.eg (A. Abdallah). 1All Authors have equally contributed.and scripts, this highlights the need for research in the field of developing large-scale handwriting recognition systems."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,5,"During the last thirty years researchers have been made different types of handwriting text recognition for many languages like English [1113], Russian [14,15], Arabic [16,17], Malayalam [18], Japanese [19], etc. Any language has a huge number of words. For example, The Oxford dictionary for the English language contains more than 300,000 words. A dictionary for the Kazakh language has more than 380,000 words [20], so it seems impossible to collect a handwritten word database that includes all words. As far as we know, for the Kazakh language, there is no available public dataset. In our research, we describe a large dataset, called Kazakh Offline Handwritten Text Dataset (KOHTD) to address challenging detection and recognition issues of handwritten Kazakh text in the scanned documents. We present a new Kazakh database for offline handwriting recognition. The dataset is written in Cyrillic and shares the same 42 characters in Kazakh."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,6,"This dataset is a collection of exam papers from students. There are approximately 922 010 symbols in the KOHTD dataset and 140 335 segmented images. KOHTD is suggested for many https://doi.org/10.1016/j.image.2022.116827 Received 5 October 2021; Received in revised form 21 June 2022; Accepted 12 July 2022 Available online 16 July 2022 0923-5965/ 2022 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.N. Toiganbayeva, M. Kasem, G. Abdimanap et al. Signal Processing: Image Communication 108 (2022) 116827 Fig. 1. Examples of images in our dataset. reasons. First, this dataset can serve researchers in the field of handwriting recognition issues by using deep and machine learning. Second, it is also a standard and pure dataset for evaluating and comparing different algorithms performances. Third, there is no available dataset in the Kazakh language."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,7,"Our database consists of a large collection of exam papers filled by students at Satbayev University and Al-Farabi Kazakh National University, this exam was made and answered in the Kazakh Language (99%) and Russian Language (1%) as shown in Fig. 1, after we received this exam answer, we scanned it and make experiments that related to pre-processing of the examination lists to automatically identifying lists, evaluate the contours of lists, recovering rotations, and also segmentation by line and by words so we can apply our Deep Learning model to recognize each word and remove the artifacts in the edges at the boundaries of segmented words. We have developed our intelligent software using state-of-the-art deep learning models to solve the problem of recognizing and processing natural language, which consists of optical character recognition of the manuscript texts in Kazakh and Russian languages."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,8,"The main contribution of our research is summarized as follows: First, This paper introduces the KOHTD dataset, a novel dataset for the Kazakh language. Our dataset includes 3000 handwritten exam papers, 140335 segmented images, and about 922010 symbols. Second, we present a brief description of datasets and deep learning models for handwritten recognition and present comparative results. For a better understanding of models performance, CER, WER, SER metrics are used to test each model. Third, we built many robust baselines using state-of-the-art models with end-to-end deep neural networks to test the effectiveness of our dataset. We compared handwritten recognition models like Bluche [21], Puigcerver [22], Flor [23], Abdallah [24]. The following section defines the related work on Handwriting Databases and Deep Learning models for handwritten. Section 3presents the Data collection and storage phases as one of the most timeconsuming and costly stages."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,9,"Section 4 provides Dataset segmentation. Section 5 provides Experiment Result on the KOHTD dataset and conclusion and future work are given in Section 6. 2. Related work 2.1. Existing datasets IAM dataset [25,26] is a handwritten sentence for the English language. The database can be used for handwritten recognition problems. This database is made on LancasterOslo/Bergen (LOB) Corpus. The IAM Handwriting Database 3.0 is made by 657 different writers and contains 1539 scanned handwritten pages with 5685 labeled sentences and 13,353 labeled text lines with a total of 115,320 labeled words, these database has been used in offline handwriting recognition [2729], handwritten text segmentation [30,31] and writer identification [32,33]. RAMIS [34] is a database of an industrial application. The main reason to develop the database was to collect handwritten samples similar to those sent by postal mail and fax by individuals to different companies."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,10,"The database was filled by 1300 volunteers who contributed to the data collection, providing 5605 mails that contain 12,723 pages. Every mail contains two to three pages, including the letter written by the volunteer, a form of the letter information, and an optimal fax sheet. Then the pages were scanned and the database was published to support testing of the tasks such as mail classification [35], handwritten recognition [36], and writer recognition [37]. The HKR [14] is a database of Russian and Kazakh texts that can be used to address detection and recognition problems, the database has 95% Russian and 5% Kazakh words/sentences, It is written in Cyrillic and share 33 characters and there are 9 additional characters for Kazakh alphabet. The dataset is consisting of more than 1500 forms. The database contains about 63,000 sentences which are more than 2N. Toiganbayeva, M. Kasem, G. Abdimanap et al. Signal Processing: Image Communication 108 (2022) 116827 715,699 symbols."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,11,"The HKR database was written by approximately 200 different writers. The IFN/ENIT [38] is a database of handwritten Arabic town/village names. The forms are filled by 411 writers with nearly 26 400 names that contain more than 210 000 characters. IFN/ENIT database contains 26 459 handwritten Tunisian town/village names. The database is developed for training and determining handwritten Arabic word recognition systems. KHATT [16] is a database of Arabic handwritten text, it can be used for Arabic offline handwritten text recognition. KHATT is consisting of 1000 handwritten forms that are written by 1000 different writers. These forms are scanned at 200,300 and 600 dpi resolutions, the database contains 2000 randomly selected paragraphs which consists of 9327 lines. These forms were randomly divided into 70% for training, 15% for testing, and 15% for verification. The database was employed in text recognition, writer identification, and verification."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,12,"HIT-MW [39] is a database for Chinese handwriting text, it can be used for offline Chinese handwritten text recognition problems. The current version of the HIT-MW database contains 853 forms and 186,444 characters. The database is collected by postal mail and middleman not face to face, it can serve many applications concerning real handwriting recognition. Parzival [40] database contains 47 pages of a medieval manuscript with 4477 text lines, 23,478 word instances, 4934 word classes, 93 letters authored by three authors in the thirteenth century. This database has 96 distinct characters. One of the most important epic works of the European Middle Ages, written in Middle High German on parchment with ink. Washington [40] database has 20 pages, 656 text lines, 4894word instances, 1471-word classes, and 82 letters handwritten by two writers in the 18th century. Although the text is written in longhand script and the graphics are binarized, the language is English."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,13,"SHIBR [41] includes a digital image dataset of historical handwritten birth records kept in the archives of many parishes around Sweden, as well as the metadata that facilitates the performance evaluation of document analysis algorithms. SHIBR is the name of the dataset (the Swedish Historical Birth Records). It is the first and largest openaccess Swedish dataset of its sort in the country (15,000 high-resolution color images of the era between 1800 and 1840). They conduct some data mining on the dataset to extract statistics and information that genealogists would find valuable. Also provide a comprehensive review of publicly accessible contemporary datasets on the topic, as well as a succinct overview of word detection methods. Each picture has 17 columns of data in the text transcription file. As a consequence, the dataset might be utilized in document analysis competitions such as word detection."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,14,"Saint Gall [42] database, which contains images as well as a transcription of a Latin manuscript written in Carolingian script from the 9th century. When compared to the handwritten image, the available transcription is of great quality for a human reader, however, the spelling of the words is not exact. As a result, the transcription presents various alignment issues, such as line breaks, abbreviations, and capitalization. Also present a character Hidden Markov Modelsbased alignment system that can handle these issues and efficiently aligns whole document pages. Saint Gall database can be used for training recognition systems. ESPOSALLES [43],this study introduces a novel database derived from a collection of marriage license booklets. Marriage license books have been used by ecclesiastical organizations to register marriage licenses for ages. This collection contains handwritten books that span about half a millennium to the turn of the twentieth century."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,15,"A study of the capabilities of state-of-the-art handwritten text recognition systems when applied to the supplied database is also offered. the dataset is useful for helping in the development of automatic handwriting recognition software for historical documents holding social records. Germana [44], the goal of this study is to make it easier to compare alternative techniques to text line extraction and offline handwritingTable 1 The table illustrates a quantitative comparison of the existing datasets in handwritten recognition."
