64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,17,"It is also ideal for evaluating interactive handwriting recognition algorithms in a realistic setting. RODRIGO [45] is a handwritten text database. On the other hand, RODRIGO is based on a much older text, dated from 1545, and exhibits the typical flaws of historical documents. We methodically documented every text block, line, and transcription from a vocabulary of 17k words, resulting in about 20k lines and 231k running words. This projects main purpose is to increase academic awareness of this annotation and to help with handwriting recognition challenges. CArDIS [46] offers Character Arkiv Digital Sweden (CArDIS), a new publicly accessible image-based Swedish historical handwritten character and word dataset (https://cardisdataset.github.io/CARDIS/). The samples in CArDIS were taken from 64,084 Swedish historical texts published between 1800 and 1900 by different unidentified clergymen."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,18,"The Swedish alphabet dataset has 116,000 RGB color pictures with 29 classes, whilst the word dataset contains 30,000 image samples of 10 popular Swedish names as well as 1000 Swedish geographical names. EMNIST [47] dataset has become a typical benchmark for computer vision, learning, and classification systems. The tasks comprehensible and straightforward character, its minimal size and storage needs, and the databases accessibility and ease of use contribute to its broad acceptance. The MNIST database was created from the NIST Special Database 19, which comprises numerals, uppercase, and lowercase handwritten letters. Table 1 presents a comparison between popular datasets of handwritten recognition. this table show the number of pages, lines, words, writers and language in each dataset. 2.2. Handwritten text recognition classifiers Approaches to handwritten text recognition can be classified into the following categories: Techniques based on HMMs and approaches based on RNNs."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,19,"For cursive text recognition, HMM-based approaches have a number of advantages. HMM, models are resistant to noise and can tolerate variations in writing; there are automated algorithms for training the HMM models, and the HMM tools are freely available. Cursive text segmentation is error-prone and time-consuming, which is not required by HMM. Bunke [27] proposes a system for offline recognition of unconstrained handwritten texts with a wide vocabulary. Only one assumption is made regarding the data: it is written in English. This enables 3N. Toiganbayeva, M. Kasem, G. Abdimanap et al. Signal Processing: Image Communication 108 (2022) 116827 us to apply Statistical Language Models to improve the performance of their system. Data from single and numerous writers have been used in several experiments. Lexica of various sizes (between 10,000 and 50,000 words) were utilized. The usage of language models has been found to improve the systems accuracy."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,20,"their strategy is detailed indepth and compared to other ways for dealing with the same problem that has been given in the literature. It is suggested that an experimental configuration be used to correctly deal with unconstrained text recognition. Safabakhsh [48] uses a continuous-density variable-duration hidden Markov model, CDVDHMM [49] to present a full method for recognizing Farsi Nastaaligh handwritten words. New techniques are used in the preprocessing step to locate and eliminate ascenders, descenders, dots, and other secondary strokes from the original image after binarization, noise reduction, and linked component specification. After that, a new segmentation method based on upper contour analysis and two other processes is used. This algorithms major purpose is to avoid the problem of under segmentation. The over-segmentation problem can be solved by taking into account variable duration states in the system."
64_2022_KOHTD Kazakh offline handwritten text dataset.pdf,21,"The CDVDHMM models the sequence of obtained sub-characters by determining the right-to-left order. In the feature space, eight features are used to represent symbols, including three Fourier descriptors and five structural and discrete characteristics. This feature vector is size and shifts insensitive. Pure characters (without secondary strokes) and some compound forms of characters in the Nastaaligh handwriting style are considered in the model. AlKhateeb [50] Using Hidden Markov Models (HMMs), a wordbased offline recognition system is proposed. Preprocessing, feature extraction, and classification are the three stages of the approach. The first step is to segment and normalize the words from the input scripts. Then, using a sliding window moving across each mirrored word image, a set of intensity features is collected from each of the split words. Meanwhile, structure-like information such as the number of subwords and diacritical marks are retrieved."
