59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,1,"IEEE.org IEEE Xplore IEEE SA IEEE Spectrum More Sites Subscribe Conferences >2021 IEEE International Confe... Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings Extracted From well-known Face Recognition Models Publisher: IEEE Cite This PDF Rassul Tolegenov; Kairat Bostanbekov; Daniyar Nurseitov; Kuanysh SlyamkhanAll Authors 1 Cites in Paper177 Full Text V iewsDonate Cart Create Account    Alerts Manage Content Alerts Add to Citation Alerts  Abstract Document Sections I.INTRODUCTION DEEP LEARNING BASED F ACE RECOGNITION MODEL EXPERIMENTS AND EVALUA TION DISCUSSION AND CONCLUSION Authors Figures References Citations Keywords Metrics More Like This  Downl PDFAbstract: This paper demonstrates a qualitative evaluation/comparison of face embeddings extracted from deep learning models, such as VGG-Face, Dlib, and OpenFace, on a face discri..."
59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,2,"View more Metadata Abstract: This paper demonstrates a qualitative evaluation/comparison of face embeddings extracted from deep learning models, such as VGG-Face, Dlib, and OpenFace, on a face discrimination task. While conducting experiments, each of linear SVM (support vector machine) classifier , Euclidean distance, and Cosine distance algorithms was utilized to compare/analyze face vectors (embeddings) extracted from those 3 deep learning models. This resulted in 9 overall combinations of face recognition techniques to be compared. To implement a fair comparison of these 9 combinations, first, training and test datasets were gathered; these datasets were made up of complete frontal and well-cropped (NxN sized) face images of 33 persons (mostly Asian), with at least 10 dif ferent face images for each person. Then, face images in the training dataset were introduced into deep learning models to extract face vectors from them."
59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,3,"Next, these face vectors were stored in a local directory as a reference database (to be used with Euclidean and Cosine distance methods) and were used to train SVM classifier. Subsequently , these face vectors were utilized to classify (recognize) face images (vectors) from the test dataset. As experiments proved, the best face recognition technique amongst 9 combinations was Dlib based face recognition model (with SVM classifier combined) as it showed the highest rate to distinguish people from each other .Although, this research work does not bring novelty to the domain, it took an ef fort to evaluate/compare well-known deep face models performances on Asian faces (mostly) and choose the best one to utilize as a basis for door access control application."
59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,4,"Published in: 2021 IEEE International Conference on Smart Information Systems and Technologies (SIST) Date of Conference: 28-30 April 2021 Date Added to IEEE Xplore : 29 June 2021DOI: 10.1109/SIST50301.2021.9465952 Publisher: IEEE ADVANCED SEARCHAll Browse My Settings Help  Institutional Sign In Institutional Sign InPersonal Sign In 03.05.2024, 14:08 Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings Extracted From well-known Face Recognition Models | IEEE Conference Public https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9465952 1/4More Like This Face Recognition Based on Principal Component Analysis and Support Vector Machine Algorithms 2021 40th Chinese Control Conference (CCC) Published: 2021 Building an Extensive Database for Training Predictive Models in Image Classication of Mammography Views and Projections using Support Vector Machines 2023 20th International Conference on Electrical Engineering, Computing Science and Automatic Control (CCE) Published: 2023 Show MoreISBN Information:Conference Location: Nur-Sultan, Kazakhstan Authors  Figures  References  Citations  Keywords  Metrics I."
59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,5,"INTRODUCTION Face recognition task has been a main focus for a multitude of research work within Computer Vision field in recent decades [22], [23], [24], [25]. The main goal in this task is to detect a face (person) from an image or video frames coming from a video stream, extract face features distinct to that face, and identify/classify that face (person). Starting from 1960s (during 1964-1965, pioneers of automated face recognition W oody Bledsoe, Helen Chan W olf, and Charles Bisson started working on their human face recognition project), there have been developed many algorithms to recognize human faces."
59_2021_Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings.pdf,6,"These include traditional facial features and landmarks based algorithms [1], [19], [20], [21], [22], skin texture analysis [13] and so on.Sign in to Continue Reading Contents 03.05.2024, 14:08 Qualitative Evaluation of Face Embeddings Extracted From well-known Face Recognition Models | IEEE Conference Public https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9465952 2/4IEEE Personal Account CHANGE USERNAME/P ASSWORDPurcha se Details PAYMENT OPTIONS VIEW PURCHASED DOCUMENTSProle Inform ation COMMUNICA TIONS PREFERENCES PROFESSION AND EDUCA TION TECHNICAL INTERESTSNeed Help? US & CANADA: +1 800 678 4333 WORLDWIDE: +1 732 981 0060 CONT ACT & SUPPOR TFollow  About IEEE Xplore | Contact Us | Help | Accessibility | Terms of Use | Nondiscrimination Policy | IEEE Ethics Reporting  | Sitemap | IEEE Privacy Policy A not-for-profit organization, IEEE is the world's largest technical professional organization dedicated to advancing technology for the benefit of humanity."
